// N114: fused decode / verify QSA attention for Intel Xe2 (Arc Pro B70) as a torch XPU op library
// (torch.ops.n114qsa.*), XPU-graph capturable (no host sync, every per-step scalar read on the device, launch shape a
// function of (rows, index width) only, scratch via at::empty).
//
// One op replaces, per QSA layer and decode step, SGLang's non-CUDA paged path
//   expand_qsa_block_indices (torch, ~20 kernels)  ->  _logical_to_physical (torch, ~8 kernels; exl3xpu maps through
//   req_to_token in graph mode)  ->  qsa_sparse_attention (exl3xpu: torch reference in capture, ~15 kernels)
// with two kernels:
//   1. chunk kernel, one work-group per (row, kv head, split): each thread derives its cell's logical token
//      (compressed block * ratio + offset masked to < seq_len, or one of the ratio - 1 pending-tail tokens, exactly as
//      torch_expand_qsa_block_indices) and physical slot (table[row_of(seq), logical], valid iff 0 <= logical <
//      row_len[seq], exactly as _logical_to_physical), then scores the chunk's cells for the kv head's 12 query heads
//      (fp32), runs an online softmax across the split's chunks and accumulates P.V (fp32);
//   2. log-sum-exp merge of the splits (Strata attn_merge_kernel), bf16 output (RNE).
// Index-taking mode (expand = 0) skips the expansion and treats the [R, W] input as logical token indices.
//
// Semantics = SGLang qsa_sparse_attention_reference over the expanded slots: softmax over each row's valid slots only,
// a row without a valid slot outputs exact 0, GQA q head h reads kv head h / 12, duplicate cells count twice.
// Precision: fp32 scores (exact products of bf16 q and fp8/bf16 k), fp32 softmax (exp2, log2(e) folded into the
// scale) and accumulation; the torch reference that graph decode runs today rounds scores and P to bf16.
//
// Structure (chunk kernel) = the n107-qsa/N108 "bcast" kernel (lane-per-cell Q.K with the q slice broadcast lane by
// lane, chunk softmax, P.V with one thread per dimension) generalised to chunks of 64 / 128 / 256 cells: with CH < 256
// cells the 256 / CH dimension quarters of a cell are scored by different sub-groups and summed in SLM, so every
// sub-group works on small decode chunks. The split-K layout (one chunk per work-group by default) and the merge are
// Strata's qsa_decode_attn_batch (sycl/src/kernels/cuda/qsa_decode_attn.dp.cpp).
//
// fp8 e4m3fn KV decode: mode 0 exact integer decode to fp32; mode 1 bits -> fp16 (exact; the 256 is folded into the q
// scale and the output normalisation).
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Portions (split-K chunk layout, the merge kernel, the per-query decode attention design) derived from Strata
// (github.com/Niko1221/Strata, HEAD 82f46a8):
//
// MIT License
